From ba93f202e44a305463e6452ebbbe445563e6ca56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:09:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The law battery gets a clock it can finish, and the box's
 absent clocks come back

data/law_gate.json on the trading box was 270 h old and held 14 of 56 fences, which is forty
"fence_ran" defects and, by L1.49, every green claim resting on those fences uncashable. Nothing
had been disabled and nothing had failed: full_gate gives each of 56 fences up to 600 s, so one
battery can cost nine hours, and a gate that cannot fit an hourly window does not run at all.

run_law_gate.py --rotate runs the fences that have gone longest without a verdict until its
budget is spent and merges them into the record, which now carries each fence's own ran_at and
the 48 h window it must be inside. A verdict older than the window is DROPPED, so a fence that
stops running is reported as never run rather than carried green. Measured on the first pass:
18 fences in 120 s, so the hourly 1800 s budget covers the battery several times over. No fence
was disabled and no bar lowered: the pass ships RED with the real breaches named.

MT5-LawGate (hourly at :40) is its clock. MT5-CycleNoon, MT5-CycleMidnight, MT5-RebootDrill and
MT5-ShadowSync were declared by the installer and absent from the scheduler; they are registered
from their own declared triggers and scripts. MT5-PlumbingWatchdog is installed from its own
installer. MT5-Gateway and MT5-ArtifactSync leave the manifest with their reasons: the gateway
runs as MT5-GatewayResident (measured: gateway_state.json 32 s old at the time of writing), and
the installer deliberately unregisters ArtifactSync because the VPS it fed was decommissioned.

MT5-AdoptRelease's window goes 20 -> 50 minutes. The adoption was being KILLED by its own limit
mid `git merge -s ours` -- "could not write index / fatal: stash failed", exit 267014 -- which
is why the box sat 9 commits behind, running code that was not the shipped code. The same pass
with no limit adopted 24,297 paths and reached the tip.

